squo;s 6 grids runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them, more than any other pair. In 2025, August to September came in at 45% of normal on the middle of the grids, and November to December at 47%. This year so far, April to May reads 135% of normal for 2026 on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1988, with grid 24743 at 44% that year.</p>"}
